# Match the original

This is a 1:1 reimplementation of Lemmings Revolution. The stock 640x480 executable is the authority.

## Separate observations from hypotheses

Say which is which, in notes and in code. `Rules` in `src/sim/World.h` labels each field MEASURED or PROVISIONAL. Do not promote a guess because it is plausible or because classic Lemmings used it.

- Measured: a climber's world Y stepped 34.190, 35.190, 36.190, one world unit per 200 ms tick, so `climbSpeed` is 2 mask rows.
- Hypothesis, still provisional: `fallSpeed = 3`. The hatch and a walk-off share one fall speed, and that step size has not been read.

## Support the conclusion

A claim about the original needs an address and what was read there, a code reference, or a harness script someone can run again.

- `0x004C36A0` is the click hit-test. The drawn crosshair is the doubles at `0x004CBFB0` +0x170 and +0x178.
- `measure_motion.centroid` is world height. The screen pair is the projection.
- `tools/harness/check_mask.py` and `measure_motion.py` are re-runnable.
- Anti-grav is cell bit `0x8000` (round 9): corpus 18/18 with `anti_grav.a3d`,
  walk probe at `0x0041C154`, gravity flip at `0x0042F5E3`. Re-run
  `measure_antigrav.py --audit` / `--enter m06_kf_1 --watch-only`. The bit
  alone is not enough — painting `0x8000` onto MM_CLIMB_002 without an
  anti-grav object flipped nothing. `compare_tick.py` is superseded; use
  `measure_steppers.py --compare` and the actor list at `0x004CBB18`.
